.DS_Store

# Release binaries and signing keys are never committed.
#
# The APKs belong on GitHub Releases, not in the tree. The upstream project
# committed its own signed APK here, which meant this repository carried a 13 MB
# binary signed by a key nobody here controls — indistinguishable at a glance
# from a release of this fork.
#
# The keystore is the one file whose loss cannot be undone: lose it and the app
# can never be updated for anyone who already installed it. It belongs outside
# the repository, backed up twice, with its password and alias stored separately.
*.apk
*.jks
*.keystore

# Review documents.
#
# The audit reports are written against one revision and read once. Committing
# them would put a snapshot of the code's problems beside the code, where it
# goes stale the moment anything is fixed — and fixing it is the whole point of
# writing the report. They belong on the machine that produced them.
AUDIT*.md
